      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2013 Mosby, Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Serum retinol-binding protein 4 (RBP4) has been proposed as a metabolic risk factor in obesity. We found that RBP4 levels also were associated with liver enzymes and cystatin C. Oxidant stress is a significant feature in obese children with greater values of RBP4 that can mediate the development of comorbidities."
      },
